    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We want to find the number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles from a bag of 7 different colored marbles. Since each marble is different, we are looking at permutations.\n\nThis is a combination problem because the order of the marbles does not matter, we are choosing marbles regardless of the order (recall that 3 objects can only be ordered in 3! = 3 × 2 × 1 = 6 ways).\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 marbles from 7 is $\\binom{7}{3} = \\boxed{35}$.Answer.",
